
-lt – Used to check whether one number is less than another number.

shift – Used to remove the first argument and shift the remaining arguments to the left.

for file in "$@" – Used to execute the loop for each remaining file argument.

-f – File test operator used to check whether a file exists and is a regular file.

sed -i – Used to edit the file in-place by overwriting the original file with the changes.

"/$word/d" – Used to search for the specified word and delete the entire line containing it.

"$file" – Represents the filename stored in the variable.

done – Used to mark the end of the for loop.
